note A comprehension in round brackets is an aggregate: this is the operation
note `price` applied to a list of items, not a list of prices. The checker
note catches it because `price` takes one item.
note Expected diagnostic: `price` takes an Item, not a list; for a list of prices write [price of item for each item in items].
to prices of items
    given items is a List of Item
    let prices be (price of item for each item in items)
